                </>
              </article>
            ))
          }
        </div><div class="support-needs">
          <h3>Practical support for the next tests</h3><p>
            MGS-1 / characterized simulant · refractory materials · mirror
            hardware · linear motion hardware · pyrometry · thermal camera
            access · mechanical testing · machining / fabrication ·
            environmental test equipment · engineering review.
          </p><p class="quiet">
            Equipment access, a well-designed test or a careful engineering
            review can be as useful as funding. <a href="/support"
              >Existing project support information ↗</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section
      class="shell section"
      id="research-log"
      aria-labelledby="log-title"
    >
      <div class="section-top">
        <p class="eyebrow">06 / RESEARCH LOG</p><span class="meta"
          >{logEntries.length} PUBLISHED {
            logEntries.length === 1 ? 'ENTRY' : 'ENTRIES'
          }</span>
      </div><h2 id="log-title">
        The roadmap is the hypothesis.<br />The log is the evidence.
      </h2><p class="intro">
        Plans and results belong in separate records. The original kickoff is
        preserved below. No completed material tests, sensor traces or validated
        autonomous capabilities are reported in the current published log.
      </p><div
        class="log-status-key"
        aria-label="Experiment status definitions"
      >
        <span class="tag">PLANNED</span><span class="tag">BUILDING</span><span
          class="tag">TESTING</span
        ><span class="tag pass">COMPLETE</span><span class="tag fail"
          >FAILED / LEARNED</span
        ><p>
          Status vocabulary for future experiments. These tags are not claims
          that each stage has been reached.
        </p>
      </div>
      <details class="full-details">
        <summary>What a useful experiment record should contain</summary><p>
          Every run should have an experiment ID, configuration, simulant batch,
          process variables, photographs / video, sensor traces, result, failure
          observations and a next experiment. Preserve failures when they teach
          us something; keep planned runs separate from completed measurements.
        </p><a
          class="text-link"
          href="/research/sintering/experiment-record.md"
          download>Download the experiment-record template ↓</a>
      </details>
      <div class="log-entries">
        {
          renderedEntries.length === 0 && (
            <p class="callout">
              No published log entries yet. Planned experiments are described in
              the roadmap above.
            </p>
          )
        }{
          renderedEntries.map(({ entry, Content }) => (
            <article class="log-entry" id={`log-${entry.slug}`}>
              <header>
                <>
                  <div class="log-entry-meta">
                    <>
                      <span class="tag">
                        {entry.slug === 'sintering-bricks-kickoff'
                          ? 'PLANNED · KICKOFF'
                          : 'RESEARCH RECORD'}
                      </span>
                      <time datetime={entry.data.pubDate.toISOString()}>
                        {dateFormat.format(entry.data.pubDate)}
                      </time>
                    </>
                  </div>
                  <h3>{entry.data.title}</h3>
                  <p>{entry.data.description}</p>
                </>
              </header>
              {entry.data.videos.length > 0 && (
                <div class="log-media">
                  {entry.data.videos.map(video => (
                    <figure>
                      <video
                        controls
                        preload="metadata"
                        src={video.src}
                        poster={video.poster}
                      >
                        Your browser does not support embedded video.{' '}
                        <a href={video.src}>Download the video</a>.
                      </video>
                      {video.caption && (
                        <figcaption>{video.caption}</figcaption>
                      )}
                    </figure>
                  ))}
                </div>
              )}
              {entry.data.images.length > 0 && (
                <div class="log-media image-grid">
                  {entry.data.images.map(image => (
                    <figure>
                      <img src={image.src} alt={image.alt} loading="lazy" />
                      {image.caption && (
                        <figcaption>{image.caption}</figcaption>
                      )}
                    </figure>
                  ))}
                </div>
              )}
              <div class="log-content">
                <Content />
              </div>
            </article>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="closing section">
      <div class="shell closing-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">POPULATION MARS / SOLAR REGOLITH PROGRAM</p><h2>
            Build the process.<br />Measure it.<br /><span
              >Automate what works.</span>
          </h2><p>We know enough to build the next experiment.</p>
        </div><div>
          <a class="button primary" href={expertise}
